agents/ — generic executor subagents
=======================================
(File is extensionless on purpose: the agent loader scans *.md, and a
README.md without agent frontmatter risks a startup-breaking parse error.)

What lives here
---------------
One file per model. Every agent is a GENERIC executor: the model is pinned,
the role comes entirely from the task prompt. There are no role-specialized
agents — specialization via static prompts plus dynamic briefs caused
instruction conflicts, and scaled as models × roles instead of models.

Naming: <model-slug>-<tier>. Tiers are COST, not capability:
  -free   no-cost models (6)
  -lite   budget paid, currently deepseek-v4-pro only
  -paid   flagship paid (glm, kimi, qwen)
Dots in model ids become hyphens; a redundant trailing -free is collapsed
(e.g. mimo-v2-5-free, not mimo-v2-5-free-free).

Prompt: two sentences (executor frame + follow the task prompt). Deliberately
minimal — output formats and specs belong in per-task briefs, which is where
the review-orchestration and adviser-chat skills put them.

Permissions (identical on all files — least privilege, read-only posture)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Executors observe and report; only the primary acts. Allowed: read tools,
instructions/ + /tmp/ dirs, git read-only subcommands (plain and `git -C`
forms), and read-only text tools (cat/head/tail/wc/sort/uniq/cut/tr/jq/rg/grep,
space-required form so bare invocations can't hang on stdin). Denied: edit
(covers writes), all other bash, webfetch/websearch.
Rationale: edit-without-execution can corrupt but cannot self-verify, and no
current role (advise/review/audit) needs writes or network. `sed`/`awk`/`find`/
`xargs`/interpreters/network tools stay denied: their safe and destructive
modes are indistinguishable by prefix. Verified live: chained commands
(`git status; echo X`) are denied despite prefix match — the allowlist is
enforced, not theater.

Adding a model
--------------
1. Copy the nearest-tier file. Set `model:` to the exact provider/model id and
   rewrite the one-line description ([TIER] + blurb + generic-executor line).
2. Keep the permission block and two-sentence prompt byte-identical.
3. Add the new `subagent_type` to the Tiers list in
   ../skill/review-orchestration/SKILL.md (full names only — short names do
   not resolve).
4. Restart opencode (agents/skills/permissions load at startup).

Retiring a model: delete its file, remove it from the skill tier list,
restart. If in doubt, keep the file — a stale roster entry costs nothing
until invoked, while a missing one breaks saved prompts that name it.
